# Drafted by Gemini (R18 garden), edited.

~ bed_find
Narrator: A single patch of bright yellow sunflowers stands defiant in the grey mold, smelling faintly of warm summer loam. A wooden stake beside the stalks bears the name Gwenna in smeared charcoal.
quest hb_gwennas_garden found
set hb_garden_found
* Tend the bed. -> tend
* Dig it up and carry it away. -> move
* Burn it. -> burn_ask
* Leave it as it is. -> END

~ tend
Narrator: The dark soil around the roots is crusted with pale, creeping threads of fungus, thirsty for clean water.
* [Nature DC 13] Tend it with water and care. -> tend_ok | tend_fail
* Water it from your own flask. -> tend_ok

~ tend_ok
approve tobin_hayward +3 delphine_ravelle +1: You shared clean water to save Gwenna's sunflowers
Narrator: The heavy golden heads lift ever so slightly toward the dark sky as the clean water sinks into the loam.
set hb_garden_tended
set hb_garden_outcome = "tended"
quest hb_gwennas_garden done
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil remembers the hand that turned it, even when the rest of the field goes to rot.
-> END

~ tend_fail
Narrator: Your fingers bruise the brittle stems, and the yellow petals flinch back from the creeping spores.
-> bed_find

~ move
Narrator: You work your fingers deep into the cold earth, lifting the tangled root-ball free of the encroaching grey mold.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unregistered agricultural transport from a quarantined zone is a clear municipal liability.
* [if item:seed_jar] Carry it in the seed jar. -> move_ok
* Carry it in a sack. -> move_ok

~ move_ok
Narrator: The sunflowers settle into their new cradle of dark soil, safe from the thirsty rot of the clearing.
set hb_garden_moved
set hb_garden_outcome = "moved"
quest hb_gwennas_garden done
-> END

~ burn_ask
Narrator: You hold a spark near the dry, golden leaves, where the smell of summer still lingers against the damp.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Oh, what a dreary, dreadful desecration, to ash the only gold left in this ghastly grey gallery!
* [ends:hb_gwennas_garden] Burn it for the commune's sake. -> burn
* Not after all. -> bed_find

~ burn
approve delphine_ravelle -3 tobin_hayward -3: You burned the last living sunflowers in the clearing
Narrator: The bright petals curl and blacken in the flame, leaving only a bitter smudge of ash upon the grey moss.
set hb_garden_burned
set hb_garden_outcome = "burned"
quest hb_gwennas_garden lost
-> END
